From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 06:23:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: Add the GMAC0 Ethernet
 controller

The A733 has a GMAC210 Ethernet controller, GMAC0, with its RGMII
signals on port H. The device tree does not describe it.

Add GMAC0: the MAC registers at 0x04500000, the glue registers at
0x04508000 and the interrupts GMAC0_TOP, TX and RX of channel 0 and LPI.
The glue register sits in the reset domain of RST_BUS_GMAC0, which the
binding calls "ahb"; the stmmac reset is the AXI one.

Add the RGMII pin group, function 5 on PH0-PH14. PH3 and PH15 are left
out: RGMII with the internal transmit clock does not use them.

GMAC1 is left out.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; dwmac-sun55i probes
GMAC0, reads user ID 0x20 and Synopsys ID 0x53, and the TX and RX
interrupts of channel 0 serve the iperf3 traffic.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 34 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index 19d26bafbb32..11776d44e3ac 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -405,6 +405,15 @@ mmc2_pins: mmc2-pins {
 				bias-pull-up;
 			};
 
+			/omit-if-no-ref/
+			rgmii0_ph_pins: rgmii0-ph-pins {
+				pins = "PH0", "PH1", "PH2", "PH4", "PH5",
+				       "PH6", "PH7", "PH8", "PH9", "PH10",
+				       "PH11", "PH12", "PH13", "PH14";
+				allwinner,pinmux = <5>;
+				function = "gmac0";
+			};
+
 			uart0_pb_pins: uart0-pb-pins {
 				pins = "PB9", "PB10";
 				allwinner,pinmux = <2>;
@@ -577,6 +586,31 @@ mmc2: mmc@4022000 {
 			#size-cells = <0>;
 		};
 
+		gmac0: ethernet@4500000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-gmac210",
+				     "snps,dwmac-5.20";
+			reg = <0x04500000 0x8000>,
+			      <0x04508000 0x1000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 172 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 178 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 173 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 174 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
+			interrupt-names = "macirq", "eth_lpi",
+					  "tx-queue-0", "rx-queue-0";
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_GMAC0>, <&ccu CLK_MBUS_GMAC0>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_GMAC_PTP>;
+			clock-names = "stmmaceth", "mbus", "ptp_ref";
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GMAC0_AXI>, <&ccu RST_BUS_GMAC0>;
+			reset-names = "stmmaceth", "ahb";
+			status = "disabled";
+
+			mdio0: mdio {
+				compatible = "snps,dwmac-mdio";
+				#address-cells = <1>;
+				#size-cells = <0>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		r_ccu: clock-controller@7010000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-r-ccu";
 			reg = <0x07010000 0x230>;
